# Comms visual system

Companion to [`comms-module.mdc`](comms-module.mdc). Spec: [`docs/modules/COMMS_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md`](../../docs/modules/COMMS_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md).

## Hard rules

1. **Read tokens** via `resolveCanvasTokens(brandKit)` from `useBrandStore` — do not hardcode a new full-bleed centered primary column when `CanvasTypeBlock` / `CanvasQrPlate` / `CanvasBrandHeader` fit.
2. **Style packages set tokens only** (`solid` / `field` / `workshop`). Tool layout IDs (meeting rails, solidarity stack/split, graphic notice/results) stay per-tool.
3. **Legacy default:** omit `BrandKit.canvas` → resolver matches classic layout chrome (center / flat / white-card QR) with Brand Kit typeface defaults (Montserrat + Source Sans). Do not surprise density/alignment of existing kits.
4. **Capture-safe:** inline hex/rgba inside export roots; `CanvasGrainOverlay` uses PNG tile + soft-light (never SVG `feTurbulence` alone). Duotone photos via `CanvasDuotonePhoto` (grayscale + multiply/screen).
5. **QR modules:** black on white only. Tokenize plate chrome (`qrPlate`), not module colours.
6. **Multi-union:** no OPSEU hex/names in new primitives — Brand Kit colours only.
7. **Ink:** `pickContrastingInk` / `BrandLogo backgroundColor` as in `comms-module.mdc`.
8. **Typefaces:** Brand Kit `headlineFontId` / `bodyFontId` via [`canvas-fonts.ts`](../../src/lib/comms/canvas-fonts.ts); self-hosted OFL only (`next/font/local`). Apply `tokens.headlineFontFamily` / `bodyFontFamily` on capture type. Flyer may override with `inherit` or a catalog id.
9. Update the migration register in `COMMS_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md` when a family ships.

## Do not

- Invent one-off white `#FFFFFF` QR plates when `CanvasQrPlate` exists
- Load webfonts from a CDN (ADR-014 — chrome stays system; canvas faces via `next/font/local` only)
- Collapse all tools into one layout engine
- Brand-tint QR modules without an explicit product ticket
- Hardcode Arial / Impact on export roots when Brand Kit tokens exist
